---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const title = "Legal Disclaimer - Medical Malpractice Lawyer Near Me";
const description = "Legal Disclaimer for Medical Malpractice Lawyer Near Me. Important legal notices and disclaimers regarding our website and services.";
const lastUpdated = "December 6, 2025";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/disclaimer/">
  <Header />
  <main class="legal-page">
    <div class="container">
      <article class="legal-content">
        <h1>Legal Disclaimer</h1>
        <p class="last-updated">Last Updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
        
        <div class="important-notice">
          <h2>⚠️ Important Legal Notice</h2>
          <p><strong>Medical Malpractice Lawyer Near Me is NOT a law firm and does NOT provide legal advice.</strong> This website is a directory service that helps connect potential clients with medical malpractice attorneys. Please read this entire disclaimer carefully before using our services.</p>
        </div>
        
        <section>
          <h2>1. No Attorney-Client Relationship</h2>
          <p>Use of this website does not create an attorney-client relationship between you and Medical Malpractice Lawyer Near Me. No attorney-client relationship is formed until you have:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Contacted and communicated directly with an attorney</li>
            <li>The attorney has agreed to represent you</li>
            <li>You have signed an engagement or retainer agreement</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Simply browsing this website, submitting inquiries, or viewing attorney profiles does NOT establish any professional relationship.</p>
        </section>
        
        <section>
          <h2>2. No Legal Advice</h2>
          <p>The information on this website is for general informational purposes only and should NOT be considered legal advice. Legal advice can only be given by a licensed attorney who has:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Been informed of all the relevant facts of your situation</li>
            <li>Conducted appropriate legal research for your jurisdiction</li>
            <li>Agreed to represent you in the matter</li>
          </ul>
          <p><strong>Do not rely on information from this website to make legal decisions.</strong> Always consult with a qualified attorney for your specific situation.</p>
        </section>
        
        <section>
          <h2>3. No Endorsement of Attorneys</h2>
          <p>The listing of attorneys on this website does not constitute an endorsement or recommendation. We do NOT:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Guarantee the competence, quality, or results of any attorney</li>
            <li>Recommend any attorney for any particular case</li>
            <li>Verify all information provided by listed attorneys</li>
            <li>Assume responsibility for any attorney's actions or advice</li>
          </ul>
          <p>You are solely responsible for selecting and evaluating any attorney you choose to contact.</p>
        </section>
        
        <section>
          <h2>4. No Guarantee of Results</h2>
          <p>Every medical malpractice case is unique. Past results do not guarantee future outcomes. The outcome of any case depends on many factors, including:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>The specific facts of your case</li>
            <li>Available evidence</li>
            <li>Applicable laws in your state</li>
            <li>Statute of limitations</li>
            <li>Many other factors</li>
          </ul>
          <p>No attorney can guarantee a specific result in any case.</p>
        </section>
        
        <section>
          <h2>5. Information Accuracy</h2>
          <p>While we strive to provide accurate information, we make no warranties about:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>The accuracy, completeness, or timeliness of attorney information</li>
            <li>Attorney credentials, ratings, or reviews</li>
            <li>Contact information for listed attorneys</li>
            <li>Any other content on this website</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Information may change without notice. Always verify important details directly with attorneys.</p>
        </section>
        
        <section>
          <h2>6. State Bar Regulations</h2>
          <p>Attorney advertising and referral services are regulated by state bar associations. This website operates in compliance with applicable rules. However:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Rules vary by state</li>
            <li>Some states may have specific requirements for lawyer directories</li>
            <li>Attorneys are responsible for their own compliance</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        
        <section>
          <h2>7. Statute of Limitations Warning</h2>
          <p><strong>IMPORTANT:</strong> Medical malpractice claims are subject to strict time limits called statutes of limitations. These vary by state and typically range from one to three years. If you believe you have a medical malpractice claim, you should:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Contact an attorney immediately</li>
            <li>Do not delay, as you may lose your right to file a claim</li>
            <li>Preserve all medical records and evidence</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Failure to act within the applicable time limit may permanently bar your claim.</p>
        </section>
        
        <section>
          <h2>8. Limitation of Liability</h2>
          <p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, Medical Malpractice Lawyer Near Me and its owners, operators, affiliates, and agents shall not be liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages arising from:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Your use of or inability to use this website</li>
            <li>Any attorney services obtained through this website</li>
            <li>Any information provided on this website</li>
            <li>Any actions or omissions of listed attorneys</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        
        <section>
          <h2>9. External Links</h2>
          <p>This website may link to external sites not operated by us. We are not responsible for the content, accuracy, or practices of any linked websites.</p>
        </section>
        
        <section>
          <h2>10. Jurisdictional Issues</h2>
          <p>This website provides information about attorneys across all 50 U.S. states. Each state has different laws regarding medical malpractice. Information that applies in one state may not apply in another. Always consult with an attorney licensed in your state.</p>
        </section>
        
        <section>
          <h2>11. Contact</h2>
          <p>If you have questions about this Disclaimer, please contact us at: legal@medicalmalpracticelawyernearme.com</p>
        </section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-page { padding: 4rem 0; }
  .legal-content { max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .legal-content h1 { font-size: 2.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .last-updated { color: #666; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  
  .important-notice { background: #f5f5f5; border: 2px solid #000; border-radius: 1rem; padding: 2rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .important-notice h2 { margin-top: 0; }
  .important-notice p { margin-bottom: 0; }
  
  .legal-content section { margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .legal-content h2 { font-size: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; margin-top: 2rem; }
  .legal-content p { color: #444; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .legal-content ul { padding-left: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .legal-content li { color: #444; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
</style>
